      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/pareiodon_cf_microps_en/",
      "html": "<p>This pencil catfish is a relative of the parasitic catfishes and is very rarely traded. Its affiliation to the genus Pareiodon is fairly clear, but the species identification has not yet been clarified.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<ul><li>Common name: none</li><li>Size: 13 cm total length</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/pareiodon_cf_microps_en/",
      "html": "<p>As predators, they should not be kept with small fishes. Due to their rarity, no reports about their maintenance in the aquarium are available. For collectors of rarities: there is one albino.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/10c-catfishes-remaining-catfish-from-south-america/pareiodon_cf_microps_en/",
      "html": "<p>Origin: Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<p>This species is monotypic (the only member of its genus) and is endemic to the Amazon river basin in Peru and Brazil. South America: Amazon river basin. Type locality: Borba, Rio Madeira, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<p>A well planted tank with a fine grained substrate and a few hiding places.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<p>Live, frozen, flake and tablet foods. Not a fussy eater.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<p>Known to bite the fins and scales of other fish in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "scotcat",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.scotcat.com/trichomycteridae/pareiodon_microps.htm",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: the specific name microps means a small appearance.</p><p>IUCN Red List: despite the little information available on this species, it is assessed as Least Concern due to its wide range (IUCN 2023).</p>"
    },
